('127.823.d.5.C',3,'A student connects the regulators, hoses, check valves and torch and tests for leaks with soapy water. This is:','["dismantling", "cleaning", "assembling the components for oxy-fuel cutting", "packing"]'::jsonb,2,'Assemble then test.','original'),
('127.823.d.5.C',4,'A common way to check a connection for gas leaks is with:','["paint", "a paper towel", "an open flame", "a soapy water solution"]'::jsonb,3,'Bubbles reveal leaks.','original'),
('127.823.d.5.D',3,'Before piercing, cutting a straight line or cutting a bevel, a student sets the tip, pressures and torch angle for the job. This is:','["proper set-up for cutting techniques", "a shutdown", "a cleanup", "a delay"]'::jsonb,0,'Set-up per technique.','original'),
('127.823.d.5.D',4,'To cut a bevel, the torch is tilted to:','["vertical only", "the angle required for the joint preparation", "a random angle", "upside down"]'::jsonb,1,'Match the angle.','original'),
('127.823.d.5.E',3,'Looking at two cut edges, one smooth and square and the other gouged with heavy drag lines, a student decides which is acceptable. She is:','["painting edges", "drilling holes", "evaluating acceptable and unacceptable cuts", "bending metal"]'::jsonb,2,'Evaluate cut quality.','original'),
('127.823.d.5.E',4,'Deep gouges and rounded top edges on a cut usually show:','["cold weather", "too much light", "a perfect cut", "incorrect speed or tip condition"]'::jsonb,3,'Cut defects have causes.','original'),
('127.823.d.6.A',3,'Before plasma cutting, Omari checks the work clamp, wears a shaded face shield and removes combustibles. He is:','["using safe operating practices", "guessing", "ignoring risks", "skipping steps"]'::jsonb,0,'Plasma safety.','original'),
('127.823.d.6.A',4,'A plasma cutter''s torch should never be pointed at:','["the floor away from people", "any person", "the work", "the table"]'::jsonb,1,'Torch discipline.','original'),
('127.823.d.6.B',3,'A cylinder stored upright, chained and capped is safe. A cylinder lying on the floor without a cap is unsafe. This shows the difference in:','["paint choices", "tool choices", "safe and unsafe storage and handling of compressed gases", "price choices"]'::jsonb,2,'Storage matters.','original'),
('127.823.d.6.B',4,'Why must a compressed gas cylinder be secured upright?','["it saves space only", "it looks neater", "it keeps gas colder", "a falling cylinder can break the valve and become a projectile"]'::jsonb,3,'Valve damage is dangerous.','original'),
('127.823.d.6.C',3,'A student checks the air pressure, installs the correct consumables and sets the amperage for the plate thickness. This is:','["proper set-up for plasma arc cutting", "a repair", "a cleanup", "a shutdown"]'::jsonb,0,'Set-up before cutting.','original'),
('127.823.d.6.C',4,'Installing the wrong nozzle on a plasma torch can cause:','["better control", "poor cut quality and faster wear", "no change", "perfect cuts"]'::jsonb,1,'Match consumables.','original'),
('127.823.d.6.D',3,'A student cuts a straight line along a guide, pierces a hole and bevels an edge with a plasma torch. She is demonstrating:','["only grinding", "only painting", "proper plasma cutting techniques", "only welding"]'::jsonb,2,'Plasma techniques.','original'),
('127.823.d.6.D',4,'When piercing with a plasma torch, the operator tilts the torch slightly to:','["increase sparks at the operator", "stop the arc", "cool the plate", "blow molten metal away from the torch and operator"]'::jsonb,3,'Tilting protects the torch.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.A',3,'Before striking an arc on a pipe weld, Wes dries his gloves, stands on a dry mat and checks his cable ends. He is:','["using safe operating practices", "skipping steps", "ignoring risks", "guessing"]'::jsonb,0,'Stick welding safety.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.A',4,'Wet gloves are dangerous for stick welding because they can:','["insulate the arc", "conduct electricity and cause a shock", "cool the rod", "improve the grip"]'::jsonb,1,'Moisture raises shock risk.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.B',3,'A welder explains that the arc melts the base metal and the electrode, while the flux coating makes slag and a shielding gas over the pool. She is demonstrating:','["gas welding", "soldering", "shielded metal arc welding principles", "brazing"]'::jsonb,2,'SMAW basics.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.B',4,'The slag layer on a stick weld protects the bead by:','["burning the metal", "adding heat", "adding color only", "slowing cooling and keeping air away"]'::jsonb,3,'Slag protects.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.C',3,'Maya connects the ground, sets the amperage for a 3/32 in. rod, and dries the rods in a rod oven. This is:','["proper set-up for shielded metal arc welding", "a purchase", "a shutdown", "a repair"]'::jsonb,0,'Set-up details.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.C',4,'Setting the current too low for the electrode can cause:','["too much penetration", "poor penetration and a sticking rod", "a faster weld", "no heat"]'::jsonb,1,'Low amperage causes sticking.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.D',3,'For a root pass on pipe, a welder picks an E6010 and for the fill passes an E7018. She is:','["choosing by color", "choosing the cheapest", "selecting appropriate electrodes for the base metal", "choosing at random"]'::jsonb,2,'Electrode selection.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.D',4,'Low-hydrogen electrodes like E7018 are used when:','["no strength is needed", "the metal is wet", "speed alone matters", "strength and crack resistance are required"]'::jsonb,3,'Low hydrogen reduces cracking.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.E',3,'A welder runs a fillet on a T-joint and a groove weld on a beveled butt joint, matching the weld size to the print. She is performing:','["fillet and groove welds to industry-accepted standards", "painting only", "cutting only", "tack welds only"]'::jsonb,0,'Standard welds.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.E',4,'A fillet weld''s size is measured as the:','["weight of its rod", "length of its leg", "color of its slag", "time it takes"]'::jsonb,1,'Leg size.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.F',3,'A thick plate needs several layers stacked in order, cleaning between each. This is:','["a flange weld", "a spot weld", "a multiple pass weld", "a tack weld"]'::jsonb,2,'Multiple passes.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.F',4,'The first pass in a multiple pass groove weld is the:','["sealing pass only", "filler pass", "cap pass", "root pass"]'::jsonb,3,'Root first.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.G',3,'Before welding, a student bevels the plate edges, grinds off mill scale and sets the root opening. She is:','["preparing joints for welding", "painting joints", "cutting rods", "storing rods"]'::jsonb,0,'Joint prep.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.G',4,'A root opening in a groove joint allows:','["a shorter arc", "penetration to the bottom of the joint", "less penetration", "no filler"]'::jsonb,1,'Root opening aids fusion.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.H',3,'A welder warms thick carbon steel before welding and lets it cool slowly afterward. This explains:','["packing", "painting", "preheating and postheating", "cleaning"]'::jsonb,2,'Heat treatment around welding.','original'),
('127.823.d.7.H',4,'A main reason for preheating is to:','["add color", "speed cooling", "reduce current", "slow cooling and reduce cracking"]'::jsonb,3,'Preheat prevents cracks.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.A',3,'Before running wire, Luz checks the gas supply, the drive rolls and the work area for flammables. She is:','["using safe operating practices", "ignoring risks", "skipping steps", "guessing"]'::jsonb,0,'GMAW safety.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.A',4,'A hot welding gun nozzle should be:','["dunked in cold water", "handled with gloves and cooled before changing", "thrown across the shop", "touched bare-handed"]'::jsonb,1,'Hot parts burn.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.B',3,'A student explains that the machine feeds a solid wire at a set speed while an inert or mixed gas shields the molten pool. She is demonstrating:','["brazing", "gas cutting", "gas metal arc welding principles", "stick welding"]'::jsonb,2,'GMAW principles.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.B',4,'In GMAW, the voltage setting mainly controls the:','["helmet shade", "wire color", "gas cost", "arc length and bead width"]'::jsonb,3,'Voltage affects the arc.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.C',3,'After loading the spool, Noel sets the gas flow, the voltage and the wire speed for 1/4 in. plate. This is:','["proper set-up for gas metal arc welding", "repair", "tear-down", "bidding"]'::jsonb,0,'Set-up before welding.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.C',4,'Too little shielding gas flow can cause:','["no heat", "porosity in the weld", "a stronger weld", "a clean bead"]'::jsonb,1,'Gas protects the pool.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.D',3,'Welding stainless steel with GMAW, a welder picks a stainless wire and a suitable gas mix. She is:','["choosing by weight", "choosing randomly", "selecting appropriate filler metals for the base metal", "choosing the cheapest"]'::jsonb,2,'Match filler to base.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.D',4,'A good filler wire for welding mild steel is:','["ER308L only", "ER4043", "brass", "ER70S-6"]'::jsonb,3,'Common mild steel wire.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.E',3,'A student welds fillet and groove joints in flat, horizontal, vertical and overhead positions to meet a code standard. She is performing:','["welds in all positions to industry standards", "only cuts", "only tacks", "only flat welds"]'::jsonb,0,'All positions.','original'),
('127.823.d.8.E',4,'Vertical-up welding with GMAW typically uses:','["maximum heat", "lower heat settings and a controlled weave", "a backhand only technique with no weave", "no gas"]'::jsonb,1,'Control the puddle.','original'),
('127.823.d.9.A',3,'Before running flux cored wire inside, Wren turns on fume extraction and checks the work area for flammables. She is:','["skipping steps", "ignoring risks", "using safe operating practices", "guessing"]'::jsonb,2,'FCAW safety.','original'),
('127.823.d.9.A',4,'Flux cored welding makes more smoke, so the best control is:','["extra heat", "no airflow", "a closed door", "ventilation or local fume extraction"]'::jsonb,3,'Fumes need removal.','original'),
('127.823.d.9.B',3,'A student explains why self-shielded wire works outdoors and then compares bead appearance with a gas-shielded wire. She is employing and appraising:','["flux cored arc welding principles", "gas cutting", "soldering", "brazing"]'::jsonb,0,'Appraisal of FCAW.','original'),
('127.823.d.9.B',4,'Gas-shielded flux cored wire generally produces:','["more spatter", "less spatter and a smoother bead than self-shielded wire", "no fumes", "no slag"]'::jsonb,1,'Gas-shielded is cleaner.','original'),
